course: dictionary
lesson: 4289
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A greeting is something friendly you say or do when you meet someone, like «Hello» or a wave. It can be a word, a handshake, a hug or a nod. Many people feel welcome when someone greets them warmly.
explain: As a noun, greeting can also mean a good wish sent to someone, like a card. A greetings card is for birthdays and holidays. In a letter, «Dear» is the greeting at the top, so one word can mean a hello, a card, or the start of a letter.
explain: Greeting is also the -ing form of the verb greet, which means to say hello to someone. In «The class was greeting the new teacher with a cheer», greeting is a verb because it shows an action. Look at the words around it to find which job it is doing.
fact: A greeting is something friendly you say or do when you meet someone.
fact: «Ignoring friends' greetings often makes them feel hurt and less likely to include you.»
fact: Greetings change from place to place. In India and Nepal, people often press their palms together and say «Namaste».
fact: In the West Country of England, people sometimes say «Alright my lover» as a friendly greeting, even to strangers.
fact: In China, «chī le ma?» («CHR luh mah») means «have you eaten?» and is a friendly greeting from grandparents and neighbours.
exercise: «Her wave was a warm greeting for her friend across the playground.» What is the greeting in this sentence? | Her friend | The playground | Across | *A wave
exercise: «The class was greeting the new teacher with a cheer.» In this sentence, what job does greeting do? | The first line of a letter | *A verb, showing an action: saying hello | A noun, meaning a birthday card | A kind of hat
exercise: What is a greetings card for? | *Birthdays and holidays | Making a cup of tea | A test at school | Crossing the road
test: In a letter, which word is the greeting? | *Dear | Sincerely | Yours | Goodbye
test: Which greeting is answered with «Wa alaykum as-salam»? | Chī le ma? | Alright my lover | Namaste | *As-salamu alaykum
exam: «Ignoring friends' greetings often makes them feel hurt.» What does this sentence tell you about greetings? | Greetings are not important at all | Greetings are only spoken, never waved | *Greetings matter, because ignoring them can hurt people | Greetings are only for birthdays
